St. Thomas[ was] outscored 54-27 in 3-point scoring. The[ biggest] trey came with :02 left in regulation and[ the] T[oms] ahead 63[-]60 when the Auggies' Matt Carik[ sank] a tying shot[ from] deep in the corner.
The Tommies' comeback was aided by sinking 29-of-33 free throws and[ committing] just 11 turnovers in the 55-minute game.
